    "body": "I didn’t get it. In that example, https://www.example.com could just specify same-site to allow https://example.com from embedding. If it didn’t want that, then they could specify same-origin, which wouldn’t allow https://example.com from embedding https://www.example.com.\r\n\r\nWhy does cross-origin make sense here as opposed to cross-site?",
