    "created_at": "2020-03-24T07:19:26Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-03-24T07:19:26Z",
    "body": "Your logic sounds like if you specify a resource as CORP cross-origin, that resource won’t be allowed to loaded by same-origin pages.\r\nAnyways, this wasn’t a technical issue but more of a wording thing. cross-origin works, but that might confuse people in a way that, if https://www.example.com want to allow  embedding to https://example.com, https://www.example.com might set CORP to cross-origin (because it’s indeed, cross-origin), but that gives wider access to other origins.",
